{"name":"Forest Frolic","hex":"#88bb95","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"forest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dense uncultivated tract of trees and undergrowth, larger than woods.","Any dense collection or amount."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover an area with trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forest"},{"term":"frolic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Merry, joyous, full of mirth; later especially, frolicsome, sportive, full of playful mischief. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Free; liberal; bountiful; generous."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make merry; to have fun; to  romp; to behave playfully and uninhibitedly.","To cause to be merry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frolic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Frolic (brig)","blocks":[{"text":"The Frolic was a brig which sank northeast of Point Cabrillo, near Caspar, California. Historians have called it \"the most significant shipwreck on the west coast\". Its shipwreck site, later known as \"Pottery Cove\" or \"Frolic Cove\", was listed on the National Register of Historic Places as Frolic (brig) in 1991."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Point_Cabrillo_Light_Station_State_Historic_Park_-_August_2022_-_Sarah_Stierch_01.jpg/330px-Point_Cabrillo_Light_Station_State_Historic_Park_-_August_2022_-_Sarah_Stierch_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frolic_(brig)","wikidata":"Q85762197"},{"title":"Forest","blocks":[{"text":"A forest is an ecosystem characterized by a dense community of trees. Hundreds of definitions of forest are used throughout the world, incorporating factors such as tree density, tree height, land use, legal standing, and ecological function. The United Nations' Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) defines a forest as, \"Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban use.\" Using this definition, Global Forest Resources Assessment 2025 found that forests covered 4.14 billion hectares, or approximately 31 percent of the world's land area in 2025."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg/330px-Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest","wikidata":"Q4421"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Point_Cabrillo_Light_Station_State_Historic_Park_-_August_2022_-_Sarah_Stierch_02.jpg/120px-Point_Cabrillo_Light_Station_State_Historic_Park_-_August_2022_-_Sarah_Stierch_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Point_Cabrillo_Light_Station_State_Historic_Park_-_August_2022_-_Sarah_Stierch_02.jpg/250px-Point_Cabrillo_Light_Station_State_Historic_Park_-_August_2022_-_Sarah_Stierch_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Point_Cabrillo_Light_Station_State_Historic_Park_-_August_2022_-_Sarah_Stierch_02.jpg/120px-Point_Cabrillo_Light_Station_State_Historic_Park_-_August_2022_-_Sarah_Stierch_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APoint_Cabrillo_Light_Station_State_Historic_Park_-_August_2022_-_Sarah_Stierch_02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Adirondacks_2016_Cascade_mountain_hike.jpg/500px-Adirondacks_2016_Cascade_mountain_hike.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https:/